  "prose": [
    {
      "section": "There are 4 methods to use modals",
      "line": 49,
      "afterExample": null,
      "text": "| | Method | Opens/closes by | `Esc` key can close it | Locks background interactions |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Dialog&nbsp;(Recommended)](#method-1-html-dialog-element-recommended) | JavaScript | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |\n| 2 | [Popover](#method-2-html-popover) | HTML attributes | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |\n| 3 | [Checkbox&nbsp;(Legacy)](#method-3-checkbox-legacy) | Hidden checkbox | ❌ No | ❌ No |\n| 4 | [Anchor Link&nbsp;(Legacy)](#method-4-using-anchor-links-legacy) | URL parameters | ❌ No | ❌ No |\n\n> :INFO:\n>\n> Opening a modal adds a [scrollbar-gutter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/scrollbar-gutter) to the page to avoid layout shift on operating systems that have a fixed scrollbar.\n> On recent Chromium based browsers vertical scrollbar presence is detected automatically. On Safari and on mobile devices the scrollbar is displayed as overlay so there will not be gutter. On Firefox you need to detect the presence of vertical scrollbar and set the `scrollbar-gutter: stable` or `scrollbar-gutter: unset` on `:root` element yourself.\n> If you don't want to use this feature, [you can exclude `rootscrollgutter`](/docs/config/#exclude)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Method 1. HTML dialog element `recommended`",
      "line": 63,
      "afterExample": null,
      "text": "HTML dialog element is a native way to create modals. It is accessible and we can close the modal using `Esc` key.  \nWe can open the modal using JS `ID.showModal()` method and close it using `ID.close()` method.  \nThe ID must be unique for each modal."
    },
    {
      "section": "Method 2. HTML popover",
      "line": 304,
      "afterExample": 5,
      "text": "Popover is similar to dialog but it still allows focusing on the background elements. It is accessible and we can close the modal using `Esc` key.  "
    },
    {
      "section": "Method 3. checkbox `legacy`",
      "line": 365,
      "afterExample": 7,
      "text": "A hidden checkbox can control the state of modal and labels can toggle the checkbox so we can open/close the modal."
    },
    {
      "section": "Method 3. checkbox `legacy`",
      "line": 410,
      "afterExample": 9,
      "text": "### Method 4. using anchor links `legacy`\nA link adds a parameter to the URL and you only see the modal when the URL has that parameter  \nWhen modal is closed, the page will scroll to the top because of the anchor link.\nAnchor links might not work well on some SPA frameworks. If there are problems, use the other methods"
    }
  ],
